<title>BELGIUM: CCB CUTS BANK SAVINGS CERTIFICATE RATES.</title>
<headline>CCB CUTS BANK SAVINGS CERTIFICATE RATES.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian Credit</p>
<p>Communal/Gemeentekrediet (CCB) said on Wednesday it would cut</p>
<p>interest rates on its bank savings certificates from Thursday</p>
<p>October 10.</p>
<p>    MATURITY	  NEW RATE	OLD RATE</p>
<p>    one year	  2.80 pct	3.00 pct</p>
<p>    three years     3.80 pct	4.10 pct</p>
<p>    five years	4.70 pct	5.00 pct</p>
<p>CCB said it was also cutting the base rates for some</p>
<p>mortgate rates, effective immediately.</p>
<p>    Variable &quot;Formula 5+5+5+5&quot;	 6.50 pct (-50 bp)</p>
<p>    Variable &quot;Formula 10+5+5&quot;	  7.75 pct (-25 bp)</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
